  "rules": {
    "close_up": "At least 70% of the 11 GT structural rays OR valid furnished rays are <=1.5m; furnished requires >=80% valid rays. Not simply GT wall clearance.",
    "corner": "Two locally straight visible GT-FP wall patches, tangent angle 90+/-15deg, both perpendicular distances <=1.5m. Patches need not meet: a visible-corner proxy, not semantic ground truth.",
    "similar_layout": "At least one candidate >2m from GT has mean absolute difference <=0.30m from the GT-nearest FP 11-ray signature, allowing all 36 yaw bins. Structural signature similarity, not proof of identical rooms.",
    "membership": "Overlapping tags on all queries, with unclassified retained. No forced three-class assignment.",
    "failure": "Primary: XY error >1m. Joint: XY>1m OR yaw>30deg. Yaw-only: XY<=1m AND yaw>30deg.",
    "mechanism": "ray_accurate_ambiguous: predicted-vs-GT-nearest FP ray MAE<=0.30m and remote signature MAE<=0.30m. large_ray_mismatch: MAE>=0.75m AND relative MAE>=25%. Remaining cases mixed/undetermined. These are diagnostic patterns, not causal labels."
  },
  "confidence_intervals": "500 physical-position cluster bootstrap draws stratified by the 3 scenes. All yaws at a position stay together. Not an unseen-scene CI.",
  "caveats": [
    "Exploratory post-hoc TEST diagnostics only; no gate/model/threshold tuned for deployment, no query removed.",
    "A tag denotes a measurable view/geometry pattern, not a proven failure cause. Tags also occur in successful queries.",
    "Similar ray signatures need not imply semantically similar rooms; close-up and corner may themselves cause signature similarity.",
    "Furnished-vs-structural disagreement can reflect ordinary clutter/portals and is NOT proof of bad data.",
    "Frozen evaluation uses the original 10m DESDF cap. It is not silently replaced by 25m. Cap-hit prevalence is reported; no cap-change ablation or re-training was performed.",
    "Localization uses 11 angular slant rays (-50..+50deg); stored training targets are 40 camera-forward depths. GT-nearest FP signature is not the exact GT pose."
  ],
